From: Łukasz Buśko <lukasz.busko@guns4hire.cc>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 07:27:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: mediatek: mt7988a-bpi-r4-pro: add ethernet mux for WAN

The WAN 10G SerDes of the BPi-R4 Pro 8X reaches either the external
Aeonsemi AS21010 PHY (phy28) or the SFP2 cage through a passive mux
driven by the SFP2 module detect line. Describe both lanes as channels
of a "mediatek,eth-mux" attached to gmac1 so the lane is selected at
runtime instead of by a boot-time overlay.

The mux node does not repeat the module detect GPIO of the cage: the
driver asks the SFP bus referenced by its SFP channel whether a module
is present, which keeps that line a single consumer of the sfp driver.

Channel ids match the logical chan-sel GPIO value: channel 0 is the PHY
lane (also described by the gmac1 node itself, which is the state the
mux starts in), channel 1 is the SFP lane. Both channels repeat the
pcs-handle of the MAC because the phylink of the selected channel owns
the PCS of that SerDes.

The PHY channel keeps USXGMII with in-band status while the SFP channel
keeps 10GBASE-R: the PHY rate-adapts its host SerDes to the speed
negotiated on the copper side and needs the PCS in-band negotiation,
whereas a 10G SFP+ module presents a fixed-rate 10GBASE-R link that
would never complete USXGMII AN.

Based on the Bananapi BPi-R4 Pro 8X vendor device tree.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt7988a-bananapi-bpi-r4-pro-8x.dts | 34 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 34 insertions

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt7988a-bananapi-bpi-r4-pro-8x.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt7988a-bananapi-bpi-r4-pro-8x.dts
@@ -24,6 +24,40 @@
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+&eth {
+	mux: mux-bus {
+		#address-cells = <1>;
+		#size-cells = <0>;
+
+		mux1: ethernet-mux@1 {
+			compatible = "mediatek,eth-mux";
+			reg = <1>;
+			#address-cells = <1>;
+			#size-cells = <0>;
+			chan-sel-gpios = <&pio 3 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+			sfp-present-channel = <1>;
+
+			mux1_phy: channel@0 {
+				reg = <0>;
+				phy-mode = "usxgmii";
+				phy-connection-type = "usxgmii";
+				managed = "in-band-status";
+				phy-handle = <&phy28>;
+				pcs-handle = <&sgmiipcs1>, <&usxgmiisys1>;
+			};
+
+			mux1_sfp: channel@1 {
+				reg = <1>;
+				phy-mode = "10gbase-r";
+				phy-connection-type = "10gbase-r";
+				managed = "in-band-status";
+				sfp = <&sfp2>;
+				pcs-handle = <&sgmiipcs1>, <&usxgmiisys1>;
+			};
+		};
+	};
+};
+
 &switch16 {
 	ports {
 		port@13 {
